! <solver:p610_t3>
! NAFEMS-style pure-shear patch test (T3, single element, 3-edge loading)
!
! Geometry (right triangle):
!   1=(0,0), 2=(1,0), 3=(0,1)
!   single T3 element with vertices 1-2-3 (CCW)
!
! Loading: mode-0 direct stress sigma = [0, 0, -100] kPa (pure shear, txy=-100).
!   The hypotenuse alone cannot distinguish biaxial -100/-100 from pure-shear
!   txy=-100 on this triangle (their tractions on the (1,1)/sqrt(2) normal are
!   identical). All 3 boundary edges must be loaded with the consistent pure-
!   shear traction:
!     edge 1->2 (bottom, n = (0,-1)): T = sigma . n = ( 100, 0)
!     edge 2->3 (hyp,    n = (1,1)/sqrt(2)): T = (-100, -100)/sqrt(2)
!     edge 3->1 (left,   n = (-1,0)): T = sigma . n = (0, 100)
!   This produces a constant pure-shear stress field exactly.
!
! Closed-form (plane strain, nu = 0.25, tension-positive):
!   sxx = 0, syy = 0, txy = -100, szz = nu*(sxx+syy) = 0.
!
! BCs: fix node 1 fully and node 2 in y only (3 fixed DOFs total, 3 free DOFs:
!   ux2, ux3, uy3). Node 3 must remain free in x so the triangle can shear; the
!   biaxial-patch BC pattern (3 fix-x, free-y) would force ux3=0 and lock out
!   the shear mode entirely.
! Pseudo-elastic via large cohesion / friction so plasticity never activates.
! <BEGIN:AnalysisOptions>
! failure_criterion MohrCoulomb
! material_type Isotropic
! mesh_type T3
! solver_executable p610_t3_elastoplastic
! expected_sxx_kPa 0
! expected_syy_kPa 0
! expected_txy_kPa -100
! expected_szz_kPa 0
! tolerance_kPa 1e-3
! <END:AnalysisOptions>
! Mesh size block:
! nels nn np_types
! nels = number of elements
! nn = number of nodes
! np_types = number of material/property types
1  3  1
! Material/property block:
! phi   c     psi  gamma  E        nu    K0
! One row per material/property type declared by np_types.
! Values are consumed by the selected solver in solver-specific order.
89  1.0e10  0  0  1000000  0.25  0
! Nodal coordinate block:
! One row per node in node-number order.
! Each row is: x y
0  0
1  0
0  1
! Element connectivity block:
! One row per element in element-number order.
! The node count per row identifies the element type; first row appears to be T3 triangle.
1  2  3
! Boundary condition block:
! First line is nr = number of restrained nodes.
! Each following row is: node_id fix_x fix_y
! 0 = fixed/restrained, 1 = free.
2
1  0  0
2  1  0
! Output/watch node block:
! First line is nouts = number of nodes requested for output.
! Following row(s) list the node IDs.
3
1  2  3
! Solver control block:
! tol limit incs layers
! tol = convergence tolerance
! limit = maximum iterations
! incs = load increments
! layers = solver path/layer selector
0.0001  80  3  0
! Traction loading block:
! First line is number of traction groups.
! Each group then contains:
! mode row: mode and stress/traction parameters
! edge count: number of loaded edges
! edge rows: node IDs defining each loaded boundary edge
1
0  0  0  -100
3
1  2
2  3
3  1
